  "body": {
    "id": "thm:error-free-reduction",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "On the submodel \\(U_1=U_2=0\\) almost surely, the factorization becomes \\(F_x(s,t)=p_x\\varphi_{f,x}(s+t)\\) and \\(G_x(s,t)=p_x\\varphi_{q,x}(s+t)\\), while the identified ADRF remains \\(\\mu(a)=\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}p_xE_P[Y\\mid A=a,X=x]\\), the standard continuous-treatment g-formula.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(U_1\\)",
      "\\(U_2\\)",
      "\\(F_x\\)",
      "\\(G_x\\)",
      "\\(p_x\\)",
      "\\(\\varphi_{f,x}\\)",
      "\\(\\varphi_{q,x}\\)",
      "\\(\\mu\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal X\\)",
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(Y\\)",
      "\\(A\\)",
      "\\(X\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:paired-channel-factorization",
      "thm:adrf-identification",
      "ass:consistency",
      "ass:unconfoundedness",
      "ass:causal-mean-continuity"
    ],
    "justification": "The reduction checks that the blind-replicate construction preserves the established causal target when measurement error vanishes.",
    "gap": "The result is a required sanity reduction rather than a novelty claim.",
    "consumer": "Implementations can be unit-tested against the ordinary error-free ADRF functional.",
    "proof_tex": "On the stated submodel, \\(U_1=U_2=0\\) almost surely, so \\(\\varphi_1(s)=\\varphi_2(t)=1\\) for every \\(s,t\\).  Substitution into the paired-channel factorization gives\n\\[\n F_x(s,t)=p_x\\varphi_{f,x}(s+t),\n \\qquad\n G_x(s,t)=p_x\\varphi_{q,x}(s+t).\n\\]\nThe identification theorem is unchanged and yields, using \\(q_x=m_xf_x\\) and overlap on \\(I\\),\n\\[\n \\mu(a)=\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}p_x\\frac{q_x(a)}{f_x(a)}\n =\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}p_xE_P[Y\\mid A=a,X=x].\n\\]\nConsistency, conditional unconfoundedness, and causal-mean continuity identify the last display with \\(E_PY(a)\\) at every \\(a\\in I\\), exactly as in equation (21).  Thus the blind-replicate functional reduces to the ordinary continuous-treatment g-formula.",
